    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the sum of interior angles in a triangle:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\). This is a fundamental property of triangles.\n\n2. **Express the mean value:**\n   The mean value of a set of numbers is calculated by summing all the values and then dividing by the number of values. For the interior angles of a triangle, we have three angles.\n\n3. **Calculate the mean value:**\n   Let the measures of the three interior angles be \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). The sum of these angles is \\(a + b + c = 180^\\circ\\).\n\n   The mean value \\(M\\) of the angles is given by:\n   \\[\n   M = \\frac{a + b + c}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Substitute the sum of the angles:**\n   Substitute \\(a + b + c = 180^\\circ\\) into the formula for the mean:\n   \\[\n   M = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the expression:**\n   Perform the division:\n   \\[\n   M = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is \\(\\boxed{60^\\circ}\\).",
